          A cordless transfer pump empties a water heater or a flooded window well with no outlet nearby. A 12-volt diaphragm pump runs the faucets in an RV or van. They are different tools for different jobs, and buying the wrong one is the usual mistake. Six pumps matched to the job.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#milwaukee-2771-20"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
